      "year": 2022,
      "shift": "25 Jul 2022, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "Which of the following alkyl halides undergoes nucleophilic substitution reaction by $S_{\\text{N}}1$ mechanism most readily?",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$(CH_3)_3C-Cl$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$(CH_3)_2CH-Cl$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "$CH_3CH_2-Cl$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$CH_3-Cl$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$S_{\\text{N}}1$ reactions proceed via carbocation intermediates. The tertiary carbocation $(CH_3)_3C^+$ is highly stable due to $+I$ and hyperconjugation effects. Hence, tertiary butyl chloride $(CH_3)_3C-Cl$ undergoes $S_{\\text{N}}1$ substitution most readily."
